Date: Sat, 24 Feb 1996 19:42:15 +0000
Subject: New NetBSD/Alpha snapshot (960224) available!

I've put a new source+binary snapshot of NetBSD/Alpha up on
ftp.netbsd.org, at:

	ftp://ftp.netbsd.org/pub/NetBSD/arch/alpha/960224

Notable changes from the last source snapshot include:

	(1) Inclusion of NFSv3 client and server support code.

	    The system tries to mount NFS servers as v3, and will
	    fall back to v2 if v3 doesn't appear to be supported.
	    If that fails for some reason, or you want to force
	    a mount to be either v2 or v3, use the -2 or -3 option,
	    when mounting the file system.  see mount_nfs(8) for
	    more details.

	(2) New BIND code (4.9.3p1, or something like that), which
	    solves all the problems i've ever seen with NetBSD/Alpha's
	    BIND code.  nslookup now works.  8-)

	(3) distribution kernels now include support for the
	    PS/2-style mouse on AlphaStations and some AXPpci systems.

	(4) the kernel no longer crashes if you access /dev/mouse and
	    there's no mouse present

	(5) The X11 bell works (obviously, only on systems where X11
	    works 8-).

(1) and (2) were changes that were made by others, in the master
NetBSD sources.


I know of no reason why this snapshot shouldn't work on any of the
'supported' systems.  If you have trouble with it, (1) please send me
mail, and (2) please pester me until i respond to your mail.  I'm
really busy, and i tend to let things slip... 8-)


chris

